# Finding 1 of RESULTS.md: after the wall clock steps back, the locks of a crashed transaction
# block every writer of their keys for the length of the step. The realtime clock goes back one
# hour before step 20. PD's timestamps then keep their physical part, and TiKV judges a lock's
# time to live by that part, so the locks that anytime_crash leaves never expire within the run:
# 90 s after the heal no transaction can write the accounts. Without the step the accounts are
# writable 2.18 s after the heal. Two runs on hvx gave fp=718f926794984e13.
# expect: violation      (change to ok when the bug is fixed)
disk=none | run T=20:-3600
